This page is to nominate fresh articles to appear in the " [LINK: (Did you know) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:DYK] " section on the  [LINK: (Main Page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Main_Page]  with a "hook" (an interesting fact). Nominations that have been approved are moved to a  [LINK: (staging area) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know/Approved]  and then promoted into  [LINK: (the Queue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Did_you_know/Queue] . To update this page,  [LINK: (purge) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Template_talk:Did_you_know&action=purge]  it.


# INSTRUCTIONS FOR NOMINATORS #

[LINK: (WP:DYKNOM) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Wikipedia:DYKNOM&redirect=no]  [LINK: (WP:DYKNOM) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:DYKNOM]

If this is your first nomination, please read the  [LINK: (DYK rules) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Did_you_know#Rules]  before continuing. Further information can be found at the  [LINK: (DYK guidelines) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Did_you_know/Guidelines] .

[LINK: (Nominate an article) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Did_you_know/Create_new_nomination?withJS=MediaWiki:DYK-nomination-wizard.js]

How do I write an interesting hook?

[LINK: (Successful hooks) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Did_you_know/Statistics#All-time_DYK_page_view_leaders]  tend to have  [LINK: (several traits) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Theleekycauldron/Essays/Assessing_DYK_hooks] . Most importantly, they share a surprising or intriguing fact. They give readers enough context to understand the hook, but leave enough out to make them want to learn more. They are written for a  [LINK: (general audience) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:AUDIENCE]  who has no prior knowledge of or interest in the topic area. Lastly, they are concise, and do not attempt to cover multiple facts or present information about the subject beyond what's needed to understand the hook.

When will my nomination be reviewed?

This page is often backlogged. As long as your submission is still on the page, it will stay there until an editor reviews it. Since editors are encouraged to review the oldest submissions first, it may take several weeks until your submission is reviewed. In the meantime, please consider reviewing another submission (not your own) to help reduce the backlog (see  [LINK: (instructions below) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#Instructions_for_reviewers] ). Because of  [LINK: (WP:DYKTIMEOUT) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:DYKTIMEOUT] , a nomination should be reviewed within two months since the reviewer/promoter may agree to reject and close an unpromoted hook after that time has passed.

Where is my hook?

If you can't find the nomination you submitted to this nominations page, it may have been approved and is on the  [LINK: (approved nominations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know/Approved]  page waiting to be promoted. It could also have been added to one of the  [LINK: (prep areas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Did_you_know/Queue#Prep_areas] ,  promoted from prep to a  [LINK: (queue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Did_you_know/Queue#Queues] , or is on the main page.

If the nominated hook is in none of those places, then the nomination has probably been rejected. Such a rejection usually only occurs if it was at least a couple of weeks old and had unresolved issues for which any discussion had gone stale. If you think your nomination was unfairly rejected, you can query this on the  [LINK: (DYK discussion page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia_talk:DYK]  or with the closer, but as a general rule such nominations will only be restored in exceptional circumstances. If your nomination was promoted, but it hasn't reached the main page after two weeks, you can also query this on the DYK discussion page.


# INSTRUCTIONS FOR REVIEWERS #

Any editor who was not involved in writing/expanding or nominating an article may review it by checking to see that the article meets all the DYK criteria ( [LINK: (long enough) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Did_you_know/Guidelines#Length] ,  [LINK: (new enough) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Did_you_know/New_article] , no serious  [LINK: (editorial or content issues) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Did_you_know#contentrules] ) and the hook is cited. Editors may also alter the suggested hook to improve it, suggest new hooks, or even lend a hand and make edits to the article to which the hook applies so that the hook is supported and accurate. For more information on the DYK rules and review processes, see the  [LINK: (DYK guidelines) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Did_you_know/Guidelines]  and the  [LINK: (reviewer instructions) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Did_you_know/Reviewer_instructions] .

To post a comment or review on a DYK nomination, follow the steps outlined below:

Look through this page, Template talk:Did you know, to find a nomination you would like to comment on.

Click the "Review or comment" link at the top of the nomination. You will be taken to the nomination subpage.

The top of the page includes a list of the DYK criteria. Check the article to ensure it meets all the relevant criteria.

To indicate the result of the review (i.e., whether the nomination passes, fails, or needs some minor changes), leave a signed comment on the page. Please begin with one of the 5 review symbols that appear at the top of the edit screen, and then indicate all aspects of the article that you have reviewed; your comment should look something like the following:Article length and age are fine, no copyvio or plagiarism concerns, reliable sources are used. But the hook needs to be shortened.  If you are the first person to comment on the nomination, there will be a line :* <!-- REPLACE THIS LINE TO WRITE FIRST COMMENT, KEEPING   :*   --> showing you where you should put the comment.

Article length and age are fine, no copyvio or plagiarism concerns, reliable sources are used. But the hook needs to be shortened.

Save the page.

After the nomination is approved, a bot will automatically list the nomination page on  [LINK: (Template talk:Did you know/Approved) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know/Approved] .

If there is any problem or concern about a nomination, please consider notifying the nominator by placing {{subst:DYKproblem|Article|header=yes|sig=yes}} on the nominator's talk page.


# ADVANCED PROCEDURES #

See  [LINK: (Wikipedia:Did you know/Preparation areas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Did_you_know/Preparation_areas]  for details on verifying a hook's acceptability.

Promoters should not promote their own nomination or their own review.

When promoting hooks intended for a particular date, keep in mind that  [LINK: (when the number of available approved nominations exceeds 120 we switch to two sets per day) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia_talk:Did_you_know/Archive_169#2-a-day_after_120_approved] , and  [LINK: (when that number drops below 60 we return to one set per day) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:PermanentLink/968228818#subsectioning_to_make_it_easier_to_see] .

Select a hook from the  [LINK: (approved nominations page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know/Approved]  that has one of these ticks at the bottom post:  .

Check to make sure basic review requirements were completed.
Any outstanding issue following   needs to be addressed before promoting.

Any outstanding issue following   needs to be addressed before promoting.

Check the article history for any substantive changes since it was nominated or reviewed.

Images for the lead slot must be freely licensed. Fair-use images are not permitted. Images loaded on Commons that appear on the Main Page are automatically protected by KrinkleBot.

Hook must be stated in both the article and source (which must be cited at the end of the article sentence where stated).

Hook should make sense grammatically.

Try to vary subject matters within each prep area.

Try to select a funny, quirky or otherwise upbeat hook for the last or bottom hook in the set.

In one tab, open the nomination page of the hook you want to promote.

In a second tab, open the  [LINK: (prep set) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Did_you_know/Queue#Prep_areas]  you intend to add the hook to.

Wanna skip all this fuss? Install  [LINK: (WP:PSHAW) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:PSHAW]  instead! Does most of the heavy lifting for ya :)

For hooks held for specific dates, refer to "Local update times" section on  [LINK: (DYK Queue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Did_you_know/Queue#Local_update_times] .
Completed Prep area number sets will be promoted by an administrator to corresponding Queue number.

Completed Prep area number sets will be promoted by an administrator to corresponding Queue number.

Copy and paste the hook into a chosen slot.
Make sure there's a space between ... and that, and a ? at the end.
Check that there's a bold link to the article.

Make sure there's a space between ... and that, and a ? at the end.

Check that there's a bold link to the article.

If it's the lead (first) hook, paste the image where indicated at the top of the template.

Copy and paste ALL the credit information (the {{DYKmake}} and {{DYKnom}} templates) at the bottom

Check your work in the prep's Preview mode.
At the bottom under "Credits", to the right of each article should have the link "View nom subpage" ; if not, a subpage parameter will need to be added to the DYKmake.

At the bottom under "Credits", to the right of each article should have the link "View nom subpage" ; if not, a subpage parameter will need to be added to the DYKmake.

Save the Prep page.

At the upper left
Change {{DYKsubpage to {{subst:DYKsubpage
Change |passed= to |passed=yes

Change {{DYKsubpage to {{subst:DYKsubpage

Change |passed= to |passed=yes

At the bottom
Just above the line containing }}<!--Please do not write below this line or remove this line. Place comments above this line.-->  insert a new, separate line containing one of the following:
To [[TM:DYK/P1|Prep 1]]
To [[TM:DYK/P2|Prep 2]]
To [[TM:DYK/P3|Prep 3]]
To [[TM:DYK/P4|Prep 4]]
