Okay, the citation problems should be fixed now.  [LINK: (A.Classical-Futurist) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:A.Classical-Futurist]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:A.Classical-Futurist] )  [LINK: (00:31, 28 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-A.Classical-Futurist-20260128003100-A.Classical-Futurist-20251129000600] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

As I look back over this, the fact that the hook is still sourced to a primary and non-independent source (the subject's own video) violates  [LINK: (WP:DYKHOOK) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:DYKHOOK] , which says citations in the article that are used to support the hook fact must verify the hook and be reliable. (Emphasis added.) A hook was just  [LINK: (pulled) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Wikipedia:Main_Page/Errors&diff=prev&oldid=1335386282]  for this reason hours ago at  [LINK: (WP:ERRORS) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:ERRORS] . Given that this nomination has timed out and still has an insurmountable barrier to approval I am regretfully marking it for closure. (Other DYK reviewers -- if you want to try to fix the problem or disagree with my conclusion, I have no objection if you undo my action here and mark as approved.)  [LINK: (Dclemens1971) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Dclemens1971]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Dclemens1971] )  [LINK: (04:53, 29 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Dclemens1971-20260129045300-A.Classical-Futurist-20251129000600] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

