The hook is false. By 1971, the term snail trail is used in essentially the same sense in Moira Pearce's Upstairs at the Bull Run. I looked further in my collection; Jason Bond's Sins of the Fathers (1983; Adonis Classics) also uses this sense.  [LINK: (Urve) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Urve]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Urve] ) 20:31, 12 January 2026 (UTC) Edited  [LINK: (Urve) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Urve]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Urve] )  [LINK: (20:36, 12 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Urve-20260112203100-Lajmmoore-20260112091000] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

