Comment: I actually love ALT4, although you will likely get less views.  The reason ALT4 speaks to me is because there is a lot of discussion in writing literature about losing or destroying drafts that forces a writer to come up with something even better.  I think there's even commentary that recommends writers destroy their first draft, so losing it on the bus speaks to this kind of thing for me.  [LINK: (Viriditas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Viriditas]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Viriditas] )  [LINK: (22:38, 25 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Viriditas-20260125223800-Lajmmoore-20260119093400] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

I was going to review this, but my DYK checker is not showing this as a 5x expansion. The above comment is noted, but I'm not sure if that would count for DYK purposes. Asking  [LINK: (Nikkimaria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Nikkimaria]  for a second opinion regarding the expansion: once this is resolved, I will give this a review. I actually have a slight preference for ALT3's fact (but not the wording), but the article doesn't seem to directly state the spanking point, and in any case I think a hook about the controversy about the cover change would be better. As for ALT4, it's acceptable, but perhaps it could be revised to also mention that she had to start from scratch many years later.  [LINK: (Narutolovehinata5) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Narutolovehinata5]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Narutolovehinata5]  ·  [LINK: (contributions) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Contributions/Narutolovehinata5] )  [LINK: (02:20, 31 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Narutolovehinata5-20260131022000-Lajmmoore-20260119093400] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]
