Thank you for devoting your time to writing about this subject,  [LINK: (Onceinawhile) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Onceinawhile] . The hook is certainly interesting, but there are important issues with the article. One, lots of the content has been copied from  [LINK: (Palestinian Christians) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palestinian_Christians] . Two, there are some really awkward or simply ungrammatical sentences. Such emigration decisions of often pursuit of better living standards, primarily economically driven. does not even have a verb. Three, the article is not well organized: the lead is tiny, "Background" section a single sentence, there are lots of single-sentence paragraphs and then one huge chunk of unbroken text. Is it possible that the topic cannot be illustrated? Are there no photographs of abandoned homes or settlements, for example?  [LINK: (Surtsicna) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Surtsicna]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Surtsicna] )  [LINK: (01:26, 20 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Surtsicna-20260120012600-Onceinawhile-20260105040100] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

