Overall:  Hello, and welcome to DYK, I hope you enjoy your stay. For the "one of the greatest albums" sections, I see it being ranked on many of those lists, but I don't see anything actually say it. If some other source says so, great; if not, I would recommend changing it to "x ranked the album 70th on its list of the 73 best Israeli albums, and y ranked it..." The personnel section is also not immediately apparent to me as being sourced in the rest of the article. Are there any sources you could put at the end of each bullet that say Eti Ante was a producer and whatnot. And, I see that the eponymous song has its own well-developed article, but it would be nice to see a sentence or something briefly talking about it here. Cheers for the very good article. Hookwise, DYK has a very high bar for claiming something was "the first" or "one of the first", and I don't think ALT1 clears that. ALT0 looks interesting and it is cited, and while grammatical, I think portions of the song not being recorded their could raise some objections, so I'd add "mostly" in front of "recorded".  [LINK: (1brianm7) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:1brianm7]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:1brianm7] )  [LINK: (08:32, 23 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-1brianm7-20260123083200-Waiting_for_the_Messiah_(album)] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

