[LINK: (Comment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Template%3ADid_you_know_nominations%2FMoffat_distillery&action=edit]  or  [LINK: (view) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Did_you_know_nominations/Moffat_distillery]

[LINK: (Article history) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Moffat_distillery&action=history]

... that  [LINK: (Moffat distillery) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moffat_distillery]  have the only wood-fired stills in Scotland, used to make both moonshine and single malt whisky?

Source: "The Moffat distillery produces hand-crafted small-batch whisky...on the only wood-fired stills in Scotland." Youngman, Angela (2026). The Whisky and Gin Lover's Guide to Scotland. Philadelphia: White Owl. p. 157. [10]

Reviewed:

Comment: This is a very unusual and unique setup - most whisky distilleries in Scotland have not been direct fired for the best part of a century and those that are, use natural gas as fuel. Moffat are using a very painstaking technique. Plus, making and selling moonshine in Scotland is also very novel.

