Sorry to say, the article is not at the level it can be DYKed; it has too many small errors. From the most to least serious: 1) I cannot locate the hook in the article (I searched for 23, twenty, three and old) 2) There are unreferenced sentences at the end of numerus paragraphs, and even several entire paragraphs 3) Citations are poorly formatted, not using citation templates, not providing information about author/publisher/dates, and one of the main references [5] seems to be a book cited with no page range. 4) main article templates are not used properly 5) headings are improperly capitalized, and the maintenance template releted to this was removed without the issue being fixed  [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Walsh_brothers_(aviation)&diff=prev&oldid=1331756582] . Overall, this requires substantial rework to be at a level we can feature this on the main page. Ping me if the issues are addressed. -- [LINK: (Piotr Konieczny aka Prokonsul Piotrus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Piotrus] | [LINK: (reply here) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Piotrus]   [LINK: (11:29, 19 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Piotrus-20260119112900-Roobee11-20260113022900] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

