New enough, long enough prose section, presentable and well-developed hurricane season list article. No QPQ required or image presented. Hook is somewhat interesting, although I'd suggest shortening it as follows: ALT0a: ... that the  [LINK: (1996 Pacific hurricane season) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_1996_Pacific_hurricane_season]  generated half of the average number of  [LINK: (major hurricanes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saffir%E2%80%93Simpson_scale] ? We have a  [LINK: (WP:DYKHOOKCITE) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:DYKHOOKCITE]  problem in that the hook fact in the article (The number of tropical storms were below average; the number of hurricanes were below average, and the number of major hurricanes was half the average of four.) is sourced to this journal article, in which I cannot for the life of me find the hook fact. This needs to be addressed in the article. The sources provided in the nomination are unintelligible to an average reader and appear to require  [LINK: (WP:OR) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:OR]  to reach the nominator's conclusion. @ [LINK: (FrizzB) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:FrizzB] : Please include a reliable source for the hook fact that does not require  [LINK: (WP:SYNTH) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:SYNTH]  and make sure it's in the article as well. I would also recommend suggesting some alternative hooks in case a promoter does not find this hook interesting as it is somewhat marginal.  [LINK: (Dclemens1971) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Dclemens1971]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Dclemens1971] )  [LINK: (16:55, 26 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Dclemens1971-20260126165500-FrizzB-20260109182100] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]
 [LINK: (Dclemens1971) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Dclemens1971]  and  [LINK: (GiftedIceCream) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:GiftedIceCream] : Just to clarify, the HURDAT database is used a lot - it is technically a reliable source and is pretty straightforward (LO, TS, HU, MH are all indicators of intensity), even if it may be hard to comprehend. However, I don't find this hook interesting since all it really says is the definition of a major hurricane and the fact that this season was below-average; there are many seasons that could be nominated with this hook's framework - a better hook is needed.  [LINK: (Hurricane) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:HurricaneZeta]  [LINK: (Zeta) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:HurricaneZeta]  [LINK: (C) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Contributions/HurricaneZeta]   [LINK: (01:29, 27 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-HurricaneZeta-20260127012900-Dclemens1971-20260126165500] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]
