Hello @ [LINK: (NegativeMP1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:NegativeMP1] , sorry for the delay. I removed the paragraph about  [LINK: (Fetty Wap) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fetty_Wap]  and  [LINK: (TikTok) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TikTok]  ( [LINK: (1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=2026_is_the_new_2016&diff=prev&oldid=1333627091] ) because it did not have a reliable source, and the statement that someone "described the year as golden in her posts" also lacked a reference, which I have now corrected. I verified this here ( [LINK: (2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=insource%3A%22Hello%21+Magazine%22&title=Special%3ASearch&profile=advanced&fulltext=1&ns0=1] ) cited  [LINK: (Hello! Magazine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hello!_Magazine] , a notable source used in other articles. The image I added in the "Origin and spread" section is relevant because it visually illustrate the use of 2016-style. I also included some images to give extra context. There's any fixes or recommendations that need to address? Thank you!  [LINK: (AdobongPogi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:AdobongPogi]   [LINK: (masarap 🍛) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:AdobongPogi]   [LINK: (02:32, 29 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-AdobongPogi-20260129023200-2026_is_the_new_2016] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

