or maybe shorter:

ALT2: ... that  [LINK: (Arena) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arena_(novel)]  was the first-ever  [LINK: (Magic: The Gathering) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic:_The_Gathering]  novel?

A few minor points, some are similar to the ones from the other review:

It was the first novel set in the set in the Magic: The Gathering universe. remove "in the set": repetitive

the Dragon magazine I think the article "the" is not required.

It was the first novel in the set in the Magic: The Gathering universe. maybe simplify to "It was the first novel set in the Magic: The Gathering universe."

who penned up the next several novels I think it the "up" should be removed

Clayton Emery, a writer ..., she compared the plot remove "she"

of powerful figures and whose should it be "powerful figures, whose"

revenge on the murders of his family should this be "murderers"?

The reviewer found it a solid and engaging novel, noting that they are the first books set the sentence jumps between singular (it) and plural (they), which sounds odd  [LINK: (Phlsph7) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Phlsph7]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Phlsph7] )  [LINK: (10:52, 25 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Phlsph7-20260125105200-Arena_(novel)] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

