New enough, long enough, QPQ done. No obvious BLP issues. The concern here is the hook is not readily understandable. What does it mean to be an opposing candidate in an intra-party election, why would that cause tension with another association? The article itself is not much clearer. (The tangential question of why there are two associations for one constituency is raised, but not somethin that needs to be addressed here.) As a quick aside the lead should mention his state, especially as he was elected on a state list.  [LINK: (CMD) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Chipmunkdavis]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Chipmunkdavis] )  [LINK: (09:09, 29 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Chipmunkdavis-20260129090900-Chorchapu-20260125151700] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]
From my understanding this is akin to a  [LINK: (primary election) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primary_election]  in the United States. So, the Ammerland CDU association ran Kossendey for their candidate and the Oldenburg CDU association's  [LINK: (Werner Broll) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Werner_Broll] . It seems like the city association took offence at the rural hillbilly Ammerland candidate running against them. I don't really know how to rephrase it, do you  [LINK: (Chipmunkdavis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Chipmunkdavis]  have any ideas?  [LINK: (Chorchapu) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Chorchapu]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Chorchapu]  |  [LINK: (edits) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Contributions/Chorchapu] )  [LINK: (15:12, 29 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Chorchapu-20260129151200-Chipmunkdavis-20260129090900] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]
I see what you mean. I would rephrase then the article to note his candidacy was controversial, rather than himself. It should also be included that he lost the 1983 CDU contest, but won the 1987 CDU contest, which is if I'm understanding the article right when the dispute got serious.  [LINK: (CMD) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Chipmunkdavis]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Chipmunkdavis] )  [LINK: (08:25, 30 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Chipmunkdavis-20260130082500-Chorchapu-20260129151200] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]
