Starting review-- [LINK: (Kev) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Kevmin]  [LINK: (min) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Kevmin]   [LINK: (§) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Contributions/Kevmin]   [LINK: (18:32, 30 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Kevmin-20260130183200-2003_LN6-20260126155100] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]
 As it stands now, the expansion is new enough and long enough.  However the description section for the castes is in violation of CLOPEN rules and needs heavy revision, full phrases that are not specific un-translatable technical terms are lifted from sources. Earwig shows a 60%+ duplication with the main reference used for the morphology section.  Also, sentences are duplicated across the subsections with only changes to the data numbers, resulting in multiple duplicated links.
In addition though the entire section is making the article unbalanced.  Section tracking added to the talk page shows 2,060 words in Morphology, and only 1,028 words for the entire rest of the prose. Articles should be written for a general audience not a specialist looking to do identifications.  There should be more that can be said about the ecology and the human impacts.-- [LINK: (Kev) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Kevmin]  [LINK: (min) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Kevmin]   [LINK: (§) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Contributions/Kevmin]   [LINK: (00:49, 31 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Kevmin-20260131004900-Kevmin-20260130183200] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

As it stands now, the expansion is new enough and long enough.  However the description section for the castes is in violation of CLOPEN rules and needs heavy revision, full phrases that are not specific un-translatable technical terms are lifted from sources. Earwig shows a 60%+ duplication with the main reference used for the morphology section.  Also, sentences are duplicated across the subsections with only changes to the data numbers, resulting in multiple duplicated links.

In addition though the entire section is making the article unbalanced.  Section tracking added to the talk page shows 2,060 words in Morphology, and only 1,028 words for the entire rest of the prose. Articles should be written for a general audience not a specialist looking to do identifications.  There should be more that can be said about the ecology and the human impacts.-- [LINK: (Kev) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Kevmin]  [LINK: (min) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Kevmin]   [LINK: (§) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Contributions/Kevmin]   [LINK: (00:49, 31 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Kevmin-20260131004900-Kevmin-20260130183200] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

