 Going to do a full review. New enough (5x expansion), long enough, neutral and reliably sourced. Copyvio free; no QPQ required. Article is presentable (and is a GA nominee). On the hook:  [LINK: (Camilasdandelions) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Camilasdandelions]  What does management mean here? I assume it means her  [LINK: (talent manager) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talent_manager]  based on the source but the hook isn't clear on this; it could mean management of the record company. Also, the source doesn't she didn't receive "feedback"; it says she didn't receive "advice", which is different. (Almost all advice is feedback, but not all feedback is advice.) But I'm also skeptical of this claim because Banks' comment "This is what it's gonna be" is not particularly clear about what's going on -- when did her management hear her music? Did she send finished music directly to the record company? What was the role of her management in selling the album? Is there another source for this claim or more context in the current source? Thanks --  [LINK: (Dclemens1971) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Dclemens1971]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Dclemens1971] )  [LINK: (18:33, 29 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Dclemens1971-20260129183300-Dclemens1971-20260129052400] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]
