ALT1: ... that the  [LINK: (International Criminal Court) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Criminal_Court]  decided to switch from  [LINK: (Microsoft Office) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Office]  to  [LINK: (OpenDesk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenDesk]  after its chief prosecutor was disconnected from his Microsoft-hosted email account? Source: In response to US president  [LINK: (Donald Trump) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump] 's  [LINK: (imposition of sanctions) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Executive_Order_14203]  against the  [LINK: (International Criminal Court) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Criminal_Court]  (ICC), which was followed by the ICC's chief prosecutor  [LINK: (Karim Khan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karim_Ahmad_Khan]  being disconnected from his Microsoft-hosted email account, the ICC announced in October 2025 that it would switch from  [LINK: (Microsoft Office) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Office]  to OpenDesk. [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#cite_note-7]  [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#cite_note-8]  [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#cite_note-9]  [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#cite_note-10]

