– Hi  [LINK: (3family6) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:3family6] , I liked to review this one because I know German. Nice article, neat and polished. I will begin by saying that this is new enough (24. Jan) and meets length criteria. The hook is interesting and is indeed sourced and cited by inline ref. My suggestions are: trying to replace some of Heaven's Metal sources (no Earwig copybio detection) but the small percent is attributed to these sources. Second suggestion is to insert a "dmy" or "mdy" dates template, and a non-negotiable requirement will be a sourcing of all the Track Listing or a "selected ones" list. QPQ done and no problems beyond that.  [LINK: (CoryGlee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:CoryGlee]   [LINK: (02:13, 27 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-CoryGlee-20260127021300-3family6-20260125232600] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

Edit with a small detail – I think that "Kirchenaustritte" is not equal to resignations such as one of an ordained priest or nun, but rather is intended to mean departing or leaving the faith in the church. Anyone else with knowledge in German agree with this?  [LINK: (CoryGlee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:CoryGlee]   [LINK: (02:26, 27 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-CoryGlee-20260127022600-CoryGlee-20260127021300] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

