Free of  [LINK: (copyright violations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Copyright_violations] ,  [LINK: (plagiarism) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Plagiarism] , and  [LINK: (close paraphrasing) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Close_paraphrasing] :

Hook eligibility:

[LINK: (Cited) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Did_you_know#Cited_hook] :

Interesting:

Other problems:  - I find the hook interesting. However, even after reading the article, I'm curious about the reason why Hinsken decided to "smuggle" a red lantern. I'm also curious about the word "smuggle", which insinuates it was illegal to do so. Why was taking the lantern from one region to another considered illegal? Obviously, this shouldn't be in the hook, but I'm curious if the article text could be expanded to explain more, especially if we're guiding readers to the article based on this action.

Overall:  My only real concern is what's stated above. I was curious reading the hook, and when I went to the article, I didn't receive answers to the questions I asked in my head: why did he do this? Why this gesture? What was the inspiration? Why "smuggled"?  [LINK: (Significa liberdade (she/her)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Significa_liberdade]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Significa_liberdade] )  [LINK: (22:15, 28 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know#c-Significa_liberdade-20260128221500-Ernst_Hinsken] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Did_you_know] ]

